BEHAVIOR build-output

DESCRIPTION
  Frames the consumer output into result: the 19-byte ts timestamp at offset 0,
  then the fixed  PROCESSED BY CONSUMER + newline at offsets 19..41 (frame-mid),
  then the first body_len bytes of body at offset 42. result_len is 42 +
  body_len. ts_len is expected to be 19.

CONTRACT
  INPUT ts bytes 65536
  INPUT ts_len int 8
  INPUT body bytes 65536
  INPUT body_len int 8
  OUTPUT result bytes 65536
  OUTPUT result_len int 8
  REQUIRES frame-mid@e6d87080 copy@05c62b49 add-int@506d7b8d
  GUARANTEES writes_output

HASH 8a0476f5

COMPOSITION
  ct = CALL copy ts 0 result 0 ts_len
  DISCARD ct.bytes_copied
  m = CALL frame-mid
  cm = CALL copy m.buf 0 result 19 23
  DISCARD cm.bytes_copied
  cb = CALL copy body 0 result 42 body_len
  DISCARD cb.bytes_copied
  rl = CALL add-int 42 body_len
  SET result_len rl.result
END
